3. FEATURE ONE: CLASH ARENA

Create a new game mode named CLASH ARENA.

This is an original, round-based competitive mode inspired by the general concept of small-team elimination games.

It must be distinct from the existing battle-royale mode.

Match structure

Create two teams:

- Player Team.
- Rival Team.

Each team should contain four characters when performance permits.

The player controls one character.

The remaining teammates are controlled by AI.

The rival team is also controlled by AI.

Start with a compact arena instead of reusing the entire island.

Create a fictional arena called SUNSET YARD.

Include:

- Low walls.
- Containers.
- Small buildings.
- Open lanes.
- Elevated platforms where practical.
- Clearly defined team starting areas.
- Several paths between the two sides.
- A boundary that prevents players from leaving the arena.

Use original environment geometry.

Do not copy a specific commercial game's arena layout.

Round rules

Each round should have:

- A short preparation countdown.
- A starting position for each team.
- A defined round timer.
- A win condition.
- A defeat condition.
- A transition to the next round.
- A visible score.

The primary win condition is to be the last team with active players.

If the timer expires, use a fair tiebreaker based on the remaining team's status and total remaining health.

Avoid indefinite draws.

Use a configurable match format.

Start with a best-of-five match.

The first team to win three rounds wins the match.

Round economy

At the start of each round, allow the player to select from a limited collection of fictional equipment.

Give the player a simple budget or limited selection system.

Stronger equipment should have a higher selection cost.

The economy should reset or update according to clear rules.

Do not create pay-to-win mechanics.

Required behavior

Implement:

- Team spawn positions.
- Round countdown.
- Round reset.
- Team health.
- Elimination.
- Round scoring.
- Match scoring.
- Victory screen.
- Defeat screen.
- Rematch.
- Return to lobby.

Every round must start in a clean state.

Eliminated characters must not continue participating in the next round.

The player must not be able to exploit the reset system to create duplicate characters or preserve unintended health.

If the arena mode is not yet stable, finish this mode before starting the next major feature.

